{"number": 66, "text": "                                                  and       authority\n\n                A     Health   and  safety  regulations\n\n\n                          Dear colleague,\n                          As you are probably aware, the government has recently passed new laws relating to\n                          health and safety in the workplace. These new regulations have been introduced’ to\n                          standardise  procedure in workplaces across the country and ensure that employers\n                          adhere  to standards.\n                          The enclosed guide details the steps you need to take in order to comply with these new\n                          laws. All employers have an obligation to carry out a risk assessment’. Failure to do so\n                          will leave us in breach of the law’. The purpose of the risk assessment is to minimise\n                          danger  to employees and also to make it easier for employers to satisfy the requirements\n                          of the regulations.\n                          All department heads have an obligation to read the information in the guide carefully.\n                           Please do so, and if you have any further questions, | will be happy to answer them.\n                           PA\n                           Health and Safety Officer\n\n\n                      1 also broughtin * an exercise to identify and assess risks 3 (formal) breaking the law\n\n\n                         We say: We could not arrive at an agreement or We could not reach an agreement, NOT\n                         We could not gette or We could not find an agreement.\n\n\n                B|    Planning    permission\n                      1f         ta      ea  an avtancian ta            it ic ahealutaly         ta caak nermiccinn2\n                      to do so. If your plan is approved, then you will be granted         to build. But it is becoming\n 